hypotheses.statement:
Under the hypotheses of [lemma:compression](#lemma:compression), there is a law of $X^T=(X_1,\ldots,X_T)$ and $\Gamma\in TS-TS$ such that every $X_i$ has law $U_S$, the joint law is invariant under permutations of the letters, and, with $Z=\sum_{i=1}^T X_i+\Gamma$, $$\label{eq:source-1}
 D(X^T\|U_S^{\otimes T})+\mathrm I(X^T;Z)
       +\mathbb E c(\Gamma)\le E.$$

Under the hypotheses of [lemma:compression](#lemma:compression), there is a probability law $\nu$ on $S$ and a joint law $\Psi$ of an exchangeable $T_0$-tuple with common marginal $\nu$ and an error $\Gamma\in TS-TS$ such that, writing $Z=\sum_{i=1}^{T_0}X_i+\Gamma$, $$\label{eq:source-2}
\begin{split}
 &\log|S|-\mathrm H(\nu)\le CE/T,\\
 &D(X^{T_0}\|\nu^{\otimes T_0})
       +\mathrm I(X^{T_0};Z)+\mathbb E c(\Gamma)\le CE,\\
 &\|\mathcal L_\Psi(X^m)-\nu^{\otimes m}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}
       \le C m_*\sqrt E/T\qquad(1\le m\le m_*).
\end{split}$$ All constants here are numerical.

Under the hypotheses of [lemma:compression](#lemma:compression), there is a finite sequence of context refinements from empty context to $W$, and an index $j$, such that $$\begin{split}
 G_1(\varnothing)-G_1(W)&\le\frac{CD_*^2}{Eh^2},\\
 K_{m_{j,1}}(W;r_j)&\le K_{m_{j,0}}(W;r_j)+E.
 \end{split}
 \label{entropy-refinement:search-conclusion}$$ The constant $C$ is numerical, and every context produced is finite-valued.

outputs.exact_statement:
Fix $D_0,P_0\ge1$. Let $q$ be a strictly positive probability mass function on $\mathbb Z$. Suppose that, for a positive integer $g$ and a probability measure $\omega$ on $\mathbb R/\mathbb Z$, $$\label{entropy-foundations:characteristic}
 H_q(x):=\frac{q(x)}{q(0)}
   =\int\chi_{gx}(\theta)\,d\omega(\theta),\qquad
 \chi_v(\theta)=e^{2\pi i v\theta},\qquad
 F_0:=-\log q(0)\le D_0d.$$ Let $S\subset\mathbb Z$ be finite and nonempty and assume $$\label{entropy-foundations:sumset-hypothesis}
 \log|nS|\le D_0d h^{P_0}\log d
 \qquad\text{for every integer }1\le n\le d^2.$$ Suppose $d/h^2\le E\le D_0d$ and, for every probability measure $\lambda$ on $S$, $$\label{entropy-foundations:moment-hypothesis}
 -\log\mathbb E_\lambda
 H_q(X_1+\cdots+X_T-X'_1-\cdots-X'_T)\le E,$$ where the $2T$ letters in this expectation are independent with common law $\lambda$. Then there exist $x_0\in S$ and a nonempty subset $S'\subset S$ such that $$\label{entropy-foundations:size-conclusion}
 \log|S|-\log|S'|\le C(D_0)\frac{d^2}{Eh^2}$$ and, for every probability measure $v$ on $S'$, $$\label{entropy-foundations:volume-conclusion}
 \int\exp\!\left(
   -L\sum_{x\in S'}v(x)
          (1-\operatorname{Re}\chi_{g(x-x_0)}(\theta))
              \right)\,d\omega(\theta)\ge e^{-CE}.$$ The constant $C$ in [entropy-foundations:volume-conclusion](#entropy-foundations:volume-conclusion) is numerical. The constant in [entropy-foundations:size-conclusion](#entropy-foundations:size-conclusion) depends only on $D_0$; the lower threshold for $d$ may also depend on $P_0$.

Under the hypotheses of [lemma:compression](#lemma:compression), there is a law of $X^T=(X_1,\ldots,X_T)$ and $\Gamma\in TS-TS$ such that every $X_i$ has law $U_S$, the joint law is invariant under permutations of the letters, and, with $Z=\sum_{i=1}^T X_i+\Gamma$, $$\label{eq:source-1}
 D(X^T\|U_S^{\otimes T})+\mathrm I(X^T;Z)
       +\mathbb E c(\Gamma)\le E.$$ The construction may be made with $Z\in TS$.

Under the hypotheses of [lemma:compression](#lemma:compression), there is a probability law $\nu$ on $S$ and a joint law $\Psi$ of an exchangeable $T_0$-tuple with common marginal $\nu$ and an error $\Gamma\in TS-TS$ such that, writing $Z=\sum_{i=1}^{T_0}X_i+\Gamma$, $$\label{eq:source-2}
\begin{split}
 &\log|S|-\mathrm H(\nu)\le CE/T,\\
 &D(X^{T_0}\|\nu^{\otimes T_0})
       +\mathrm I(X^{T_0};Z)+\mathbb E c(\Gamma)\le CE,\\
 &\|\mathcal L_\Psi(X^m)-\nu^{\otimes m}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}
       \le C m_*\sqrt E/T\qquad(1\le m\le m_*).
\end{split}$$ All constants here are numerical.

Under the hypotheses of [lemma:compression](#lemma:compression), fix the law $\nu$ from [entropy-foundations:exchangeable](#entropy-foundations:exchangeable). Let $m,r$ be positive integers satisfying $$m\le m_*,\qquad 2mr\le T_0,\qquad
 r\le \tfrac12 T e^{-w^2}.$$ For the constant context and for every finite refinement of it, $$\label{eq:source-3}
 K_m(W;r)\le CE,$$ where $C$ is numerical, with the threshold for $d$ allowed to depend on $D_0,P_0$.

Under the hypotheses of [lemma:compression](#lemma:compression), there is a finite sequence of context refinements from empty context to $W$, and an index $j$, such that $$\begin{split}
 G_1(\varnothing)-G_1(W)&\le\frac{CD_*^2}{Eh^2},\\
 K_{m_{j,1}}(W;r_j)&\le K_{m_{j,0}}(W;r_j)+E.
 \end{split}
 \label{entropy-refinement:search-conclusion}$$ The constant $C$ is numerical, and every context produced is finite-valued.

Consider any finite procedure starting with the type-zero label, making at most $\lfloor C_0h\rfloor$ successful main additions and using the updates of [lemma:spectral-update](#lemma:spectral-update) with its hypotheses at every attempt. Require all discrete choices to depend only on spatial prefixes and input memberships, with independent label errors given $Y$ and its parameter path, and include all the success draws specified above. Then an admissible regular attempt has the following conditional reference bound, given its past and its success coin. The observable event $$\label{eq:source-10}
 \begin{gathered}
 \text{for some fresh clone }Z',\qquad A(Z'-Z)\le4s_d,\\
 \left|\sum_x\nu(x)v_x(Z')\chi_{gx}(V)\right|\ge\beta/4.
 \end{gathered}$$ has probability at most $e^{-t/8}$, where $Z$ is the old main label. Under the true input law, all attempted pasts are admissible and [eq:source-10](#eq:source-10) occurs at every regular success simultaneously, except on a set of probability $o(h^{-20})$. This includes the label draws at a final success breaching a cap. The bounds are uniform in depth, cutoff, and the deterministic choices made at the states.

There are absolute constants $C$ and $d_0$ with the following property. Let $d\ge d_0$, put $h=\log\log d$, and let $I\subset\mathbb R$ be a half-open interval with $1/2\le |I|\le1$. Let $\rho:I\to[0,\infty)$ be measurable, with $\rho\le e^d$ almost everywhere and $$m_{\rm top}=\frac1{|I|}\int_I\rho\le2.$$ Give $I$ its normalized uniform probability $\mathbf U$. Write $\mathcal F_j$ for its depth-$j$ dyadic sigma field, $p_j(x)$ for the depth-$j$ interval containing $x$, and $r_{j+1}$ for the sign that is $+1$ on the left child and $-1$ on the right child of each such interval. Let $J\ge1$ and $Q\ge0$ be integers. For $0\le j<J$, let $\epsilon_j:I\to\mathbb C$ be $\mathcal F_{j+1}$-measurable with $|\epsilon_j|\le1$, and use the same $\epsilon_j$ for all modulations. The bits through depth $J+1$ are retained, so the last output sign is $r_{J+1}$.*

*Set $$\tau(x)=\min\bigl(\{0\le j<J:\ \mathbb E_{p_j(x)}\rho>e^{4h}\}\cup\{J\}\bigr),
 \qquad \mathbb E_p v=\frac1{|p|}\int_p v(y)\,dy,$$ and, with $\chi_u(y)=e^{2\pi iuy}$, define $$\mathcal H_{I,J}^{u}\rho(x)
 =\sum_{0\le j<\tau(x)}
       \mathbb E_{p_j(x)}[\rho(Y)\chi_u(Y)r_{j+1}(Y)]\,
       \epsilon_j(x)r_{j+2}(x).$$ Then $$\label{eq:dyadic-estimate}
 \int_I\max_{\substack{u\in\mathbb Z\\|u|\le Q}}
           |\mathcal H_{I,J}^{u}\rho(x)|\,\frac{dx}{|I|}
 \le Cd.$$ The constants are independent of $I,\rho,J,Q$, and the multipliers. Consequently the same estimate holds with $\sup_{u\in\mathbb Z}$ in place of the finite maximum.

The main and scalar snapshot lists have respectively the cardinality bounds in [prop:capture](#prop:capture). While a snapshot is current, it covers every $v\in[D]$ that is high at threshold $0.9b$ at a jumping node, with its stored separation neighborhoods measured at the snapshot’s birth interval. Moreover, if $N_{\rm snap}$ is the number of snapshots on the capped uniform output path, then $$\label{eq:07-snapshot-count}
 \mathbb E_{\mathbf U_e}N_{\rm snap}
 \le 1+D_{\max}+C b^{-6}
       +C b^{-12}\bigl(d_1+D_{\max}\log(CD_{\max}/b)\bigr).$$ Every snapshot is born before its node’s next fair bit. Its stored representatives may subsequently be used on the same plateau even after replacement of that snapshot.

Let $(r_{i+1})$ be fair signs in a filtration $(\mathcal F_i)$, and let $c_i$ be real $\mathcal F_i$-measurable coefficients. For every $\theta>0$ and $t\ge0$, outside an event of probability at most $e^{-t}$, $$\sum_{i<n}c_i r_{i+1}
 \le \frac{\theta}{2}\sum_{i<n}c_i^2+\frac{t}{\theta}
 \qquad\text{for every prefix }n.$$ The same statement holds conditionally at a stopping-time origin and with predictable stopping or masking of the coefficients. For complex sums one may apply the assertion to both signs of each real component, at a total failure probability at most $4e^{-t}$.

On $\mathbb T=\mathbb R/(2\pi\mathbb Z)$ with $d\mu=dx/(2\pi)$, set $\Phi(t)=t\log(2+t)$ and define the Luxemburg norm by $$\|f\|_\Phi
 =\inf\left\{b>0:\int_{\mathbb T}\Phi(|f|/b)\,d\mu\le1\right\}.$$ For the ordinary symmetric partial sums of [thm:main](#thm:main), put $S^*f=\sup_{N\ge0}|S_Nf|$. There is an absolute constant $C$ such that $$\label{eq:fourier-weak-l1}
 \sup_{\lambda>0}\lambda\,\mu\{S^*f>\lambda\}
 \le C\|f\|_\Phi
 \qquad(f\in L\log L(\mathbb T;\mathbb C)).$$
